WEBVTT

00:00:01.592 --> 00:00:31.244
Land of Gold by Claire Craig Copyright 2007, Newhouse and International Language Teaching Services, PTY Ltd.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:37.806
Track 3.

00:00:37.866 --> 00:00:40.698
I sit beside the pyramid.

00:00:40.758 --> 00:00:42.738
My feet are hot.

00:00:42.798 --> 00:00:47.430
Mr. Johnson is speaking about King Chios and his pyramid.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.742
I shut my eyes.

00:00:49.802 --> 00:00:53.452
Maddy, says Kate in my ear.

00:00:53.512 --> 00:00:55.422
Open your eyes.

00:00:55.482 --> 00:00:57.764
No, I say.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.814
I'm sleeping.

00:00:59.874 --> 00:01:03.606
Maddy says Kate again.

00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:06.057
I open one eye.

00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:10.469
A man is looking at us, she says.

00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:11.960
Who?

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.610
I ask.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.222
That man over there, she says.

00:01:17.282 --> 00:01:20.705
The man in the black suit.

00:01:20.765 --> 00:01:23.328
I see the man.

00:01:23.388 --> 00:01:25.638
He is looking at us.

00:01:25.698 --> 00:01:29.279
He is standing beside the pyramid.

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:33.160
He's a bad man, says Kate.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.241
I know it.

00:01:35.301 --> 00:01:38.572
Kate wants to be a detective.

00:01:38.632 --> 00:01:40.763
She reads detective books.

00:01:40.823 --> 00:01:43.584
She writes detective stories.

00:01:43.644 --> 00:01:49.382
In her stories, the bad men are always in black suits.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:53.020
No, he isn't, I say.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:56.182
He's looking at the pyramids.

00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:58.504
I am hot.

00:01:58.564 --> 00:02:01.126
I want to be in our hotel.

00:02:01.186 --> 00:02:03.568
I want to sleep.

00:02:03.628 --> 00:02:06.920
But, says Kate.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:09.573
Mr Johnson looks at her.

00:02:09.632 --> 00:02:11.714
What is it, Kate?

00:02:11.773 --> 00:02:14.246
Kate doesn't answer.

00:02:14.306 --> 00:02:20.618
She's writing stories in her head again, says Paul Hand.

00:02:20.678 --> 00:02:23.877
Mr. Johnson smiles at Kate.

00:02:23.937 --> 00:02:26.268
You and your stories.

00:02:26.328 --> 00:02:27.688
He says.

00:02:27.748 --> 00:02:30.408
Kate's face is red.

00:02:30.468 --> 00:02:32.039
Okay.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:33.119
He says.

00:02:33.179 --> 00:02:38.550
The bus is going to take us to the hotel now.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:42.620
Track four.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.751
I look at Kate and say, what?

00:02:46.811 --> 00:02:49.962
This is not my bag.

00:02:50.022 --> 00:02:51.872
She says again.

00:02:51.932 --> 00:02:55.406
It is your bag, I say.

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:58.358
No, it's not, she says.

00:02:58.418 --> 00:03:02.190
It is a brown bag, but it's new.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.722
My bag is old.

00:03:04.782 --> 00:03:06.484
Look!

00:03:06.544 --> 00:03:08.785
What's this?

00:03:08.845 --> 00:03:12.428
Kate is looking inside the bag.

00:03:12.487 --> 00:03:14.470
I go to the table.

00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:17.302
I look inside the bag too.

00:03:17.362 --> 00:03:21.258
I see a small yellow statue.

00:03:21.318 --> 00:03:24.323
It shines like the sun.

00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:29.538
Kate takes it out of the bag and puts it on the table.

00:03:29.598 --> 00:03:33.571
It is a statue of an Egyptian woman.

00:03:33.591 --> 00:03:39.696
I think she's an Egyptian queen, says Kate.

00:03:39.756 --> 00:03:42.237
Look at her clothes.

00:03:42.297 --> 00:03:45.278
Is it a gold statue?"

00:03:45.338 --> 00:03:46.698
I ask.

00:03:46.758 --> 00:03:50.120
I don't know, says Kate.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.900
She picks up the statue again.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.532
It's heavy, she says, and puts it down again.

00:03:57.592 --> 00:03:59.593
I pick it up.

00:03:59.653 --> 00:04:02.814
It is heavy, I say.

00:04:02.874 --> 00:04:07.066
Gold is heavy.

00:04:07.126 --> 00:04:11.216
Track five.

00:04:11.276 --> 00:04:12.978
Okay.

00:04:13.038 --> 00:04:14.708
Says Mr. Johnson.

00:04:14.768 --> 00:04:17.389
Get your bags and come with me.

00:04:17.449 --> 00:04:19.860
The hotel is near here.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.532
We're going to walk to it.

00:04:22.592 --> 00:04:25.232
We get off the train.

00:04:25.292 --> 00:04:28.544
We walk through the streets of Azwan.

00:04:28.604 --> 00:04:32.816
Lots of people are in the streets and in the shops.

00:04:32.876 --> 00:04:38.117
You can buy clothes and gold and silver in the shops.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.948
says Mr. Johnson.

00:04:40.008 --> 00:04:42.420
And today is market day.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:49.206
The market has stools with spices, rugs, food and coffee.

00:04:49.266 --> 00:04:56.072
The statue Kate, I say to her, are we going to tell Mr. Johnson?

00:04:56.131 --> 00:04:59.764
Yes, at the hotel, says Kate.

00:04:59.824 --> 00:05:02.057
We can tell him there.

00:05:02.117 --> 00:05:05.172
Okay, I say.

00:05:05.232 --> 00:05:08.956
We walk past the shops and stalls.

00:05:09.016 --> 00:05:11.637
I can smell the spices.

00:05:11.697 --> 00:05:14.768
I can smell coffee and food.

00:05:14.828 --> 00:05:17.999
I like the red and yellow rugs.

00:05:18.059 --> 00:05:21.410
Can we stop, please, Mr. Johnson?"

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.710
says Peter Small.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:28.354
Paul Hand is taking photos of the things in the market.

00:05:28.414 --> 00:05:30.955
Mr. Johnson looks at us.

00:05:31.015 --> 00:05:32.546
Okay.

00:05:32.606 --> 00:05:35.226
He says and smiles.

00:05:35.286 --> 00:05:38.767
Kate and I look at a shop with clothes.

00:05:38.827 --> 00:05:42.287
We look at a stool with bags of spices.

00:05:42.347 --> 00:05:48.318
We go into a shop with silver and gold.

00:05:48.378 --> 00:05:52.309
Track six.

00:05:52.369 --> 00:05:55.340
Mr. Johnson is looking at us.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.666
Your bag is missing.

00:05:57.726 --> 00:05:59.562
He says to Kate.

00:05:59.622 --> 00:06:02.054
Yes, she says.

00:06:02.114 --> 00:06:05.237
But it's not my bag.

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:10.201
And this bag has a missing statue in it?

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.093
Says Mr. Johnson.

00:06:12.152 --> 00:06:14.754
Yes, we say.

00:06:14.814 --> 00:06:19.598
And the police are looking for this man, says Kate.

00:06:19.658 --> 00:06:23.772
She gives Mr. Johnson the photo of the man in black.

00:06:23.832 --> 00:06:25.914
Look, do you see?

00:06:25.974 --> 00:06:28.112
He's taking my bag.

00:06:28.172 --> 00:06:31.670
And he's putting his bag in its place.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.222
What?

00:06:33.282 --> 00:06:35.112
says Mr. Johnson.

00:06:35.172 --> 00:06:39.984
He gives you his bag with a statue in it.

00:06:40.044 --> 00:06:41.416
Yes.

00:06:41.476 --> 00:06:45.298
He's hiding the statue, I say.

00:06:45.358 --> 00:06:51.870
The police aren't going to look for the statue in a school girl's bag, says Kate.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.235
It's a good place to hide a statue.

00:06:55.295 --> 00:06:59.470
And where is this statue now?

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.510
Says Mr. Johnson.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:04.952
He has it again, says Kate.

00:07:05.012 --> 00:07:08.172
He's here in us one too.

00:07:08.232 --> 00:07:11.364
Mr. Johnson doesn't speak.

00:07:11.424 --> 00:07:13.804
Then he smiles.

00:07:13.864 --> 00:07:17.316
It's a good story, girls.

00:07:17.376 --> 00:07:25.091
He says, the gold statue of an Egyptian queen A man in black?

00:07:25.151 --> 00:07:26.832
The police?

00:07:26.892 --> 00:07:33.086
It's a good detective story.

00:07:33.146 --> 00:07:45.766
Chapter 1 The Man in Black This is a photo of Kate and me in Egypt.

00:07:45.826 --> 00:07:47.406
I'm Maddie.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:49.812
I'm in the Red Dress.

00:07:49.872 --> 00:07:54.579
I'm standing beside Mr. Johnson, our teacher.

00:07:54.639 --> 00:07:58.680
Kate is the girl with the brown bag.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:03.053
We are in Egypt with our class from school.

00:08:03.113 --> 00:08:06.254
We are standing beside a pyramid.

00:08:06.314 --> 00:08:09.966
A camel with a big nose is behind us.

00:08:10.026 --> 00:08:13.629
The camel wants to be in the photo.

00:08:13.688 --> 00:08:17.555
Smile, says Paul Hand.

00:08:17.615 --> 00:08:21.282
We smile and Paul takes the photo.

00:08:21.342 --> 00:08:24.454
We take photos of the pyramids too.

00:08:24.514 --> 00:08:27.506
They are big in the blue sky.

00:08:27.566 --> 00:08:30.418
The sun is hot in Egypt.

00:08:30.477 --> 00:08:33.400
My face and arms are red.

00:08:33.459 --> 00:08:35.730
I have a drink of water.

00:08:35.791 --> 00:08:37.452
I look at Kate.

00:08:37.511 --> 00:08:39.764
She is hot too.

00:08:39.823 --> 00:08:43.575
Mr. Johnson is speaking about the pyramid.

00:08:43.635 --> 00:08:50.720
This is the pyramid of King Chios, a pharaoh, or king of Egypt.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:53.724
I sit beside the pyramid.

00:08:53.784 --> 00:08:55.754
My feet are hot.

00:08:55.814 --> 00:09:00.468
Mr. Johnson is speaking about King Chios and his pyramid.

00:09:00.528 --> 00:09:02.781
I shut my eyes.

00:09:02.841 --> 00:09:06.494
Maddy, says Kate in my ear.

00:09:06.554 --> 00:09:08.466
Open your eyes!

00:09:08.526 --> 00:09:10.808
No, I say.

00:09:10.868 --> 00:09:12.816
I'm sleeping.

00:09:12.876 --> 00:09:16.623
Maddy says Kate again.

00:09:16.684 --> 00:09:19.084
I open one eye.

00:09:19.144 --> 00:09:23.485
A man is looking at us, she says.

00:09:23.545 --> 00:09:24.985
Who?

00:09:25.045 --> 00:09:26.625
I ask.

00:09:26.685 --> 00:09:30.236
That man over there, she says.

00:09:30.296 --> 00:09:33.766
The man in the black suit.

00:09:33.826 --> 00:09:36.357
I see the man.

00:09:36.417 --> 00:09:38.668
He is looking at us.

00:09:38.728 --> 00:09:42.291
He is standing beside the pyramid.

00:09:42.352 --> 00:09:46.186
He's a bad man, says Kate.

00:09:46.246 --> 00:09:48.267
I know it.

00:09:48.328 --> 00:09:51.610
Kate wants to be a detective.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.791
She reads detective books.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.602
She writes detective stories.

00:09:56.662 --> 00:10:02.414
In her stories, the bad men are always in black suits.

00:10:02.474 --> 00:10:05.557
No, he isn't, I say.

00:10:05.577 --> 00:10:09.219
He's looking at the pyramids.

00:10:09.279 --> 00:10:11.531
I am hot.

00:10:11.591 --> 00:10:14.153
I want to be in our hotel.

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:16.574
I want to sleep.

00:10:16.634 --> 00:10:19.948
But, says Kate.

00:10:20.007 --> 00:10:22.600
Mr. Johnson looks at her.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.742
What is it, Kate?

00:10:24.802 --> 00:10:27.262
Kate doesn't answer.

00:10:27.322 --> 00:10:33.688
She's writing stories in her head again, says Paul Hand.

00:10:33.748 --> 00:10:36.901
Mr. Johnson smiles at Kate.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:40.712
You and your stories, he says.

00:10:40.772 --> 00:10:43.443
Kate's face is red.

00:10:43.503 --> 00:10:46.144
Okay, he says.

00:10:46.204 --> 00:10:50.065
The bus is going to take us to the hotel now.

00:10:50.125 --> 00:10:53.746
Paul Hand takes a photo of the bus.

00:10:53.806 --> 00:10:56.877
He is always taking photos.

00:10:56.937 --> 00:10:59.488
We get on the bus.

00:10:59.548 --> 00:11:01.938
I sit beside the window.

00:11:01.998 --> 00:11:04.497
Kate sits beside me.

00:11:04.557 --> 00:11:08.166
I look at the hot yellow land.

00:11:08.226 --> 00:11:11.499
Soon the pyramids are behind us.

00:11:11.559 --> 00:11:14.291
They look small now.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:17.993
The bus stops at our hotel in Cairo.

00:11:18.052 --> 00:11:22.206
The afternoon sun is hot like the morning sun.

00:11:22.266 --> 00:11:25.918
Kate takes her bag and gets up.

00:11:25.978 --> 00:11:30.950
I look out of the window and I see the man in the black suit.

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:34.170
He is standing across the street.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:38.240
A brown bag is on the ground beside him.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:41.742
He is looking at our bus.

00:11:41.802 --> 00:11:44.722
What's he doing here?

00:11:44.782 --> 00:11:46.313
I ask.

00:11:46.373 --> 00:11:47.784
Who?

00:11:47.844 --> 00:11:49.445
says Kate.

00:11:49.504 --> 00:11:50.935
Look!

00:11:50.995 --> 00:11:54.526
The man in black is across the street.

00:11:54.586 --> 00:11:56.698
She looks at him.

00:11:56.758 --> 00:11:58.188
Yes!

00:11:58.248 --> 00:12:00.540
What is he doing here?

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:01.990
She says.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:04.976
I don't like that man.

00:12:05.036 --> 00:12:07.500
We get off the bus.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.961
I look across the street again.

00:12:10.021 --> 00:12:13.772
Now I can't see the man in black.

00:12:13.832 --> 00:12:19.314
I have one photo to take, says Paul Hand.

00:12:19.374 --> 00:12:22.234
I'm going to take a photo of the hotel.

00:12:22.294 --> 00:12:26.596
Kate, Maddie, can you stand there please?

00:12:26.656 --> 00:12:30.867
Kate puts her bag on the ground behind her.

00:12:30.927 --> 00:12:34.469
We stand in front of the hotel and smile.

00:12:34.529 --> 00:12:36.630
Paul takes the photo.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.942
Thanks, he says.

00:12:39.002 --> 00:12:42.462
Now I'm going to take these to the photo shop.

00:12:42.522 --> 00:12:45.304
It's four o'clock now.

00:12:45.364 --> 00:12:47.804
Dinner is at six o'clock.

00:12:47.864 --> 00:12:49.865
Says Mr Johnson.

00:12:49.925 --> 00:12:53.436
Yes, Mr Johnson, we say.

00:12:53.496 --> 00:12:57.977
Kate takes her bag and we walk into the hotel.

00:12:58.037 --> 00:13:01.208
We go to our room and shut the door.

00:13:01.268 --> 00:13:04.511
The room is nice and cold.

00:13:04.571 --> 00:13:07.404
I sit on the bed and drink water.

00:13:07.464 --> 00:13:10.305
Kate puts her bag on the table.

00:13:10.366 --> 00:13:12.387
I'm tired.

00:13:12.448 --> 00:13:15.780
I lie down and go to sleep.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.972
I open my eyes.

00:13:18.032 --> 00:13:19.894
Kate is talking.

00:13:19.954 --> 00:13:23.617
Now, where is my book on Egypt?

00:13:23.677 --> 00:13:25.238
She is saying.

00:13:25.298 --> 00:13:27.348
It's in my bag.

00:13:27.408 --> 00:13:31.670
I want to read about the Temple of Ramesses the Great.

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:34.140
She opens the bag.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.712
We are going to go there tomorrow.

00:13:36.772 --> 00:13:39.934
It's in Arbu symbol, near Azwan.

00:13:39.994 --> 00:13:43.286
The Temple of Ramesses the Great is...

00:13:43.346 --> 00:13:46.288
She stops speaking.

00:13:46.348 --> 00:13:56.170
Maddy, she says, this is not my bag.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:14:08.482
Chapter 2 The Egyptian Queen I look at Kate and say, what?

00:14:08.542 --> 00:14:13.634
This is not my bag, she says again.

00:14:13.694 --> 00:14:17.136
It is your bag, I say.

00:14:17.196 --> 00:14:20.096
No, it's not, she says.

00:14:20.156 --> 00:14:23.918
It is a brown bag, but it's new.

00:14:23.978 --> 00:14:26.460
My bag is old.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:28.218
Look!

00:14:28.278 --> 00:14:30.506
What's this?

00:14:30.566 --> 00:14:34.148
Kate is looking inside the bag.

00:14:34.208 --> 00:14:36.189
I go to the table.

00:14:36.249 --> 00:14:39.020
I look inside the bag too.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:42.993
I see a small yellow statue.

00:14:43.053 --> 00:14:46.064
It shines like the sun.

00:14:46.124 --> 00:14:51.268
Kate takes it out of the bag and puts it on the table.

00:14:51.328 --> 00:14:56.104
It is a statue of an Egyptian woman.

00:14:56.164 --> 00:15:01.402
I think she's an Egyptian queen, says Kate.

00:15:01.462 --> 00:15:03.973
Look at her clothes.

00:15:04.033 --> 00:15:07.015
Is it a gold statue?

00:15:07.075 --> 00:15:08.436
I ask.

00:15:08.496 --> 00:15:11.858
I don't know, says Kate.

00:15:11.918 --> 00:15:14.630
She picks up the statue again.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:19.264
It's heavy, she says, and puts it down again.

00:15:19.324 --> 00:15:21.344
I pick it up.

00:15:21.404 --> 00:15:24.566
It is heavy, I say.

00:15:24.626 --> 00:15:27.517
Gold is heavy.

00:15:27.578 --> 00:15:32.678
Kate looks at the small pictures on the statue.

00:15:32.738 --> 00:15:37.651
These pictures are hieroglyphs, she says.

00:15:37.711 --> 00:15:41.753
My book on Egypt has a chapter on hieroglyphs.

00:15:41.813 --> 00:15:43.764
They are like words.

00:15:43.824 --> 00:15:46.055
They tell stories.

00:15:46.114 --> 00:15:49.376
What do these hieroglyphs say?

00:15:49.436 --> 00:15:50.806
I ask.

00:15:50.866 --> 00:15:52.087
I don't know.

00:15:52.107 --> 00:15:54.848
I can't read hieroglyphs.

00:15:54.908 --> 00:15:56.136
Kate says.

00:15:56.196 --> 00:16:01.216
My book is in my bag, and this isn't my bag.

00:16:01.276 --> 00:16:05.858
I'm going to tell Mr. Johnson about the statue, I say.

00:16:05.918 --> 00:16:08.020
No, says Kate.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.131
Don't tell Mr. Johnson.

00:16:10.191 --> 00:16:13.844
But knock, knock.

00:16:13.904 --> 00:16:17.376
We both jump and look at the door.

00:16:17.435 --> 00:16:19.728
Yes, says Kate.

00:16:19.788 --> 00:16:21.112
Who is it?

00:16:21.172 --> 00:16:23.018
It's Mr. Johnson.

00:16:23.078 --> 00:16:24.650
Come on, you two.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.361
It's six o'clock.

00:16:26.421 --> 00:16:29.113
Dinner is on the table.

00:16:29.173 --> 00:16:33.136
Kate puts the statue inside the bag.

00:16:33.196 --> 00:16:36.089
She puts the bag under her bed.

00:16:36.148 --> 00:16:38.520
We're coming, Mr. Johnson.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:39.812
She says.

00:16:39.872 --> 00:16:41.974
She looks at me.

00:16:42.034 --> 00:16:43.974
It's okay, Maddie.

00:16:44.034 --> 00:16:47.308
Mr. Johnson has a book on hieroglyphs.

00:16:47.368 --> 00:16:50.130
I'm going to ask him for it.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:55.213
Do you think the name of the queen is in the hieroglyphs?

00:16:55.273 --> 00:16:56.463
I ask.

00:16:56.523 --> 00:16:59.044
Yes, she answers.

00:16:59.104 --> 00:17:03.754
And I'm a detective, she says with a smile.

00:17:03.815 --> 00:17:08.716
A detective can find out the name of an Egyptian queen.

00:17:08.776 --> 00:17:12.626
She opens the door and walks out.

00:17:12.686 --> 00:17:15.527
The class is eating dinner.

00:17:15.587 --> 00:17:17.892
Mr. Johnson looks at us.

00:17:17.952 --> 00:17:22.680
You two are always late," he says.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:25.052
Kate smiles at him.

00:17:25.112 --> 00:17:28.154
It's Maddie, Mr. Johnson, she says.

00:17:28.214 --> 00:17:30.306
She is always late.

00:17:30.366 --> 00:17:32.566
She smiles at me.

00:17:32.626 --> 00:17:36.519
We sit beside Paul Hand and Peter Small.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:40.477
Mr. Johnson is speaking about the journey to Azwan.

00:17:40.537 --> 00:17:43.224
We have a big day tomorrow.

00:17:43.284 --> 00:17:46.336
We're going to as one by train.

00:17:46.396 --> 00:17:50.190
He says, it's a long journey.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.952
How long is the journey?

00:17:53.012 --> 00:17:54.514
Says Peter.

00:17:54.574 --> 00:17:57.046
It's about twelve hours.

00:17:57.106 --> 00:17:58.958
Says Mr Johnson.

00:17:59.018 --> 00:18:01.150
He looks at Kate and me.

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:04.693
Don't be late in the morning you two.

00:18:04.753 --> 00:18:08.057
Twelve hours on a train?

00:18:08.117 --> 00:18:12.240
Kate says to me, what are we going to do?

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.160
Look, girls!

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:16.061
says Paul Hand.

00:18:16.121 --> 00:18:18.261
I have the photos!

00:18:18.322 --> 00:18:21.683
He puts them on the table in front of us.

00:18:21.743 --> 00:18:25.574
These are the photos at the pyramids, he says.

00:18:25.634 --> 00:18:27.145
Look at the camel!

00:18:27.205 --> 00:18:30.127
He's eating your hat, Kate!

00:18:30.187 --> 00:18:37.339
We look at photos of the sky, the bus, the road, a camel, the hotel.

00:18:37.399 --> 00:18:40.200
Kate and me in front of the hotel.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.860
I look at that photo again.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:44.960
My face is hot.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.791
Kate, look at this.

00:18:47.851 --> 00:18:51.592
The photo of you and me in front of the hotel.

00:18:51.652 --> 00:18:54.202
Kate looks at it.

00:18:54.262 --> 00:18:58.513
In the photo, a man is behind Kate.

00:18:58.573 --> 00:19:01.159
He is picking up her bag.

00:19:01.219 --> 00:19:05.376
He is putting his bag on the ground.

00:19:05.436 --> 00:19:08.087
Kate's face is white.

00:19:08.147 --> 00:19:09.617
What is it?

00:19:09.677 --> 00:19:10.998
asks Paul.

00:19:11.058 --> 00:19:12.668
Don't you like the photo?

00:19:12.688 --> 00:19:15.269
No, I do.

00:19:15.329 --> 00:19:18.640
I do like this photo, says Kate.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:21.010
Can I keep it please, Paul?

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:25.062
Yes, you can keep it, says Paul.

00:19:25.122 --> 00:19:27.732
Thank you, says Kate.

00:19:27.792 --> 00:19:29.193
She looks at me.

00:19:29.253 --> 00:19:30.852
Come on.

00:19:30.912 --> 00:19:33.432
We run up to our room.

00:19:33.492 --> 00:19:36.624
We look at the man in the photo again.

00:19:36.684 --> 00:19:43.068
It is the man in black.

00:19:43.128 --> 00:19:53.685
Chapter 3 The Train to Azwan It is 6 o'clock in the morning.

00:19:53.745 --> 00:19:55.936
The sun is coming up.

00:19:55.996 --> 00:19:59.046
We are on the train to Azwan.

00:19:59.106 --> 00:20:02.156
Tyro is soon behind us.

00:20:02.216 --> 00:20:05.106
We are now in the country.

00:20:05.166 --> 00:20:07.678
I look out of the window.

00:20:07.738 --> 00:20:11.230
I see small houses and animals.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:15.192
Kate looks at the photo of the man in black.

00:20:15.252 --> 00:20:22.038
I have his bag and he has my bag, she says.

00:20:22.098 --> 00:20:24.994
What does he want your bag for?"

00:20:25.054 --> 00:20:26.486
I ask her.

00:20:26.546 --> 00:20:29.770
I don't know, says Kate.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:33.104
I'm going to ask Mr. Johnson for his book.

00:20:33.164 --> 00:20:37.439
I want to find out about the hieroglyphs on the statue.

00:20:37.499 --> 00:20:42.084
She gets up and says, See you soon.

00:20:42.144 --> 00:20:45.146
I look at the people on the train.

00:20:45.206 --> 00:20:48.398
A mother and father are sitting with their children.

00:20:48.458 --> 00:20:50.890
The boy is eating breakfast.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:53.862
The girl is reading a book.

00:20:53.922 --> 00:20:57.914
A man in front of me is reading a newspaper.

00:20:57.974 --> 00:21:03.357
I look at the words on the front page, but I can't read them.

00:21:03.417 --> 00:21:08.850
The newspaper is in Arabic, and I can't read Arabic.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:12.024
Then I see a photo.

00:21:12.084 --> 00:21:16.566
It is a photo of the gold statue.

00:21:16.626 --> 00:21:24.360
Hello, I say to the man in front of me, do you speak English?

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.912
He looks at me.

00:21:26.971 --> 00:21:29.973
Yes, he says.

00:21:30.033 --> 00:21:32.484
I do speak English.

00:21:32.544 --> 00:21:36.016
What does this story say, please?

00:21:36.076 --> 00:21:37.617
I ask him.

00:21:37.677 --> 00:21:40.508
He reads from the newspaper.

00:21:40.568 --> 00:21:43.688
Gold statue missing.

00:21:43.748 --> 00:21:48.400
A gold statue of Queen Nefertari is missing.

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:53.173
Police are looking for a man in a black suit.

00:21:53.232 --> 00:21:55.124
Thank you.

00:21:55.184 --> 00:21:57.354
I say to the man.

00:21:57.414 --> 00:22:02.048
He smiles at me and reads his newspaper again.

00:22:02.108 --> 00:22:05.228
Kate sits down beside me.

00:22:05.288 --> 00:22:07.570
Her face is red.

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:10.256
Maddie, she says.

00:22:10.316 --> 00:22:14.333
I know who the Egyptian queen is," she says.

00:22:14.393 --> 00:22:18.536
Mr. Johnson's book has a photo of the statue in it.

00:22:18.596 --> 00:22:22.379
I know who she is too, I say.

00:22:22.439 --> 00:22:27.183
Queen Nefertari, we say.

00:22:27.243 --> 00:22:30.625
It is six o'clock in the evening.

00:22:30.686 --> 00:22:34.338
The train stops at the station in Azwan.

00:22:34.398 --> 00:22:36.320
Kate is sleeping.

00:22:36.380 --> 00:22:40.118
It's a long journey from Cairo to Azwan.

00:22:40.178 --> 00:22:42.124
I open the window.

00:22:42.184 --> 00:22:44.496
The air is hot.

00:22:44.556 --> 00:22:47.450
I look up and down the station.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.092
People are getting off the train.

00:22:50.152 --> 00:22:53.134
Kate, we're here, I say.

00:22:53.194 --> 00:22:55.186
We're in Azwan.

00:22:55.246 --> 00:22:57.838
Kate opens her eyes.

00:22:57.898 --> 00:23:00.702
She looks out of the window too.

00:23:00.762 --> 00:23:02.533
Okay.

00:23:02.593 --> 00:23:04.254
Says Mr. Johnson.

00:23:04.314 --> 00:23:06.902
Get your bags and come with me.

00:23:06.962 --> 00:23:09.399
The hotel is near here.

00:23:09.459 --> 00:23:12.061
We're going to walk to it.

00:23:12.121 --> 00:23:14.774
We get off the train.

00:23:14.834 --> 00:23:18.066
We walk through the streets of Aswan.

00:23:18.126 --> 00:23:22.350
Lots of people are in the streets and in the shops.

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:27.644
You can buy clothes and gold and silver in the shops.

00:23:27.704 --> 00:23:29.495
Says Mr Johnson.

00:23:29.555 --> 00:23:31.931
And today is Market Day.

00:23:31.991 --> 00:23:38.740
The market has stalls with spices, rugs, food and coffee.

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:42.792
The statue, Kate, I say to her.

00:23:42.852 --> 00:23:45.584
Are we going to tell Mr. Johnson?

00:23:45.644 --> 00:23:49.277
Yes, at the hotel, says Kate.

00:23:49.337 --> 00:23:51.588
We can tell him there.

00:23:51.648 --> 00:23:54.740
Okay, I say.

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:58.504
We walk past the shops and stalls.

00:23:58.564 --> 00:24:01.165
I can smell the spices.

00:24:01.225 --> 00:24:04.296
I can smell coffee and food.

00:24:04.356 --> 00:24:07.528
I like the red and yellow rugs.

00:24:07.588 --> 00:24:10.939
Can we stop, please, Mr. Johnson?"

00:24:10.999 --> 00:24:13.250
says Peter Small.

00:24:13.310 --> 00:24:17.892
Paul Hand is taking photos of the things in the market.

00:24:17.952 --> 00:24:20.514
Mr. Johnson looks at us.

00:24:20.574 --> 00:24:22.084
Okay.

00:24:22.144 --> 00:24:24.775
He says and smiles.

00:24:24.835 --> 00:24:28.306
Kate and I look at a shop with clothes.

00:24:28.366 --> 00:24:31.805
We look at a stool with bags of spices.

00:24:31.865 --> 00:24:36.103
We go into a shop with silver and gold.

00:24:36.163 --> 00:24:39.744
Kate sees a small silver box.

00:24:39.804 --> 00:24:42.375
I see a gold necklace.

00:24:42.435 --> 00:24:44.726
I hold it in front of me.

00:24:44.786 --> 00:24:48.016
The necklace shines like the sun.

00:24:48.076 --> 00:24:52.678
It shines like the statue of the Egyptian queen.

00:24:52.738 --> 00:24:57.229
Then I see a man walk out of the shop.

00:24:57.289 --> 00:25:01.968
I can't see his face, but he is in a black suit.

00:25:02.028 --> 00:25:04.206
Is it him?

00:25:04.266 --> 00:25:06.457
I look for Kate.

00:25:06.517 --> 00:25:09.338
She is buying the silver box.

00:25:09.398 --> 00:25:13.749
She sees me and says, it's for my sister.

00:25:13.809 --> 00:25:16.990
Kate, where's the bag?

00:25:17.050 --> 00:25:20.581
I say, where's the statue?

00:25:20.641 --> 00:25:23.752
It's here, she says.

00:25:23.812 --> 00:25:26.502
Kate looks at the ground.

00:25:26.562 --> 00:25:29.473
The bag isn't there.

00:25:29.533 --> 00:25:32.152
Oh no, she says.

00:25:32.212 --> 00:25:33.890
Her face is white.

00:25:33.950 --> 00:25:38.811
Where is it?

00:25:38.871 --> 00:25:43.712
Chapter Four.

00:25:43.772 --> 00:25:46.382
A good story.

00:25:46.442 --> 00:25:48.943
We're in the hotel.

00:25:49.003 --> 00:25:51.693
Mr. Johnson is looking at us.

00:25:51.754 --> 00:25:54.054
Your bag is missing.

00:25:54.114 --> 00:25:55.924
He says to Kate.

00:25:55.984 --> 00:25:58.414
Yes, she says.

00:25:58.474 --> 00:26:01.228
But it's not my bag.

00:26:01.288 --> 00:26:06.562
And this bag has a missing statue in it?

00:26:06.623 --> 00:26:08.444
Says Mr Johnson.

00:26:08.504 --> 00:26:11.106
Yes, we say.

00:26:11.166 --> 00:26:15.938
And the police are looking for this man, says Kate.

00:26:15.999 --> 00:26:20.121
She gives Mr Johnson the photo of the man in black.

00:26:20.181 --> 00:26:22.272
Look, do you see?

00:26:22.332 --> 00:26:28.046
He's taking my bag, and he's putting his bag in its place.

00:26:28.106 --> 00:26:29.597
What?

00:26:29.657 --> 00:26:31.450
Says Mr Johnson.

00:26:31.510 --> 00:26:36.334
He gives you his bag with a statue in it.

00:26:36.394 --> 00:26:41.666
Yes, he's hiding the statue, I say.

00:26:41.726 --> 00:26:48.218
The police aren't going to look for the statue in a school girl's bag, says Kate.

00:26:48.278 --> 00:26:51.618
It's a good place to hide a statue.

00:26:51.678 --> 00:26:55.839
And where is this statue now?

00:26:55.900 --> 00:26:57.870
Says Mr Johnson.

00:26:57.930 --> 00:27:01.294
He has it again, says Kate.

00:27:01.354 --> 00:27:04.538
He's here in Us One Two.

00:27:04.598 --> 00:27:07.730
Mr. Johnson doesn't speak.

00:27:07.790 --> 00:27:10.172
Then he smiles.

00:27:10.232 --> 00:27:13.684
It's a good story, girls.

00:27:13.744 --> 00:27:15.134
He says.

00:27:15.194 --> 00:27:23.208
The gold statue of an Egyptian queen, a man in black, the police.

00:27:23.268 --> 00:27:26.460
It's a good detective story.

00:27:26.520 --> 00:27:31.284
Mr. Johnson, please says Kate.

00:27:31.345 --> 00:27:34.637
But Mr. Johnson walks to the door.

00:27:34.697 --> 00:27:37.900
He opens it and smiles again.

00:27:37.960 --> 00:27:42.053
We are going to go to Abu Simbal tomorrow.

00:27:42.113 --> 00:27:46.566
We are going to see the Temple of Ramesses the Great.

00:27:46.626 --> 00:27:51.701
We are going to see the Temple of his Queen Nefertari.

00:27:51.761 --> 00:27:55.254
It's going to be a long hot day, girls.

00:27:55.314 --> 00:27:57.505
Good night.

00:27:57.565 --> 00:28:04.438
I look at Kate and say, a good detective story.

00:28:04.498 --> 00:28:07.509
But this isn't a story.

00:28:07.529 --> 00:28:11.810
It isn't, says Kate.

00:28:11.870 --> 00:28:16.036
We're on the bus to Abu Simbal.

00:28:16.096 --> 00:28:17.922
I open the window.

00:28:17.982 --> 00:28:20.912
The air is hot on my face.

00:28:20.972 --> 00:28:23.283
I look in front of me.

00:28:23.343 --> 00:28:26.954
I look at the sand of the Sahara Desert.

00:28:27.014 --> 00:28:31.035
I see blue sky and yellow sand.

00:28:31.095 --> 00:28:33.926
It's a big desert.

00:28:33.986 --> 00:28:37.457
Soon we are at Arbu Symbol.

00:28:37.517 --> 00:28:41.087
We see the blue waters of Lake NASA.

00:28:41.148 --> 00:28:47.440
The temples of Ramesses the Great and Queen Nefertari are in front of us.

00:28:47.500 --> 00:28:53.432
Big statues of Ramesses the Great sit at the front of his temple.

00:28:53.492 --> 00:28:55.232
Wow!

00:28:55.292 --> 00:28:56.582
says Kate.

00:28:56.643 --> 00:29:00.214
Look at the statues of Ramesses the Great.

00:29:00.274 --> 00:29:02.404
They are big.

00:29:02.464 --> 00:29:06.186
Poor hand jumps off the bus.

00:29:06.246 --> 00:29:08.922
He takes photos of Lake Nasser.

00:29:08.982 --> 00:29:12.719
He takes photos of the big statues.

00:29:12.779 --> 00:29:17.472
We walk into the temple of Ramesses the Great.

00:29:17.532 --> 00:29:20.504
Kate speaks to Mr. Johnson.

00:29:20.564 --> 00:29:25.118
She asks him a question about Ramesses the Great.

00:29:25.178 --> 00:29:28.861
I look at the statues in the temple.

00:29:28.921 --> 00:29:34.376
Then I see him, the man in black.

00:29:34.436 --> 00:29:42.875
He is standing beside one of the statues He is speaking to a man with white hair.

00:29:42.936 --> 00:29:47.458
The brown bag is on the ground between them.

00:29:47.518 --> 00:29:50.590
Is the statue in the bag?

00:29:50.650 --> 00:29:52.801
I look for Kate.

00:29:52.861 --> 00:29:55.632
She is speaking to Paul Hand.

00:29:55.692 --> 00:29:59.314
He is taking her photo beside a statue.

00:29:59.375 --> 00:30:03.357
She is small beside the statue.

00:30:03.417 --> 00:30:07.357
The man in black walks outside.

00:30:07.417 --> 00:30:10.066
I walk outside too.

00:30:10.126 --> 00:30:14.430
He goes into the temple of Queen Nefertari.

00:30:14.490 --> 00:30:16.552
I go in too.

00:30:16.612 --> 00:30:18.963
The temple is small.

00:30:19.024 --> 00:30:21.415
The ground is dirty.

00:30:21.476 --> 00:30:23.758
The air is hot.

00:30:23.818 --> 00:30:25.799
I can't see him.

00:30:25.860 --> 00:30:27.760
Where is he?

00:30:27.820 --> 00:30:31.124
Then a hand is over my mouth.

00:30:31.184 --> 00:30:33.836
Don't speak, girl.

00:30:33.896 --> 00:30:39.214
Says a voice behind me.

00:30:39.274 --> 00:30:50.655
Chapter 5 Finding Queen Nefertari My face is hot.

00:30:50.716 --> 00:30:52.466
I am afraid.

00:30:52.526 --> 00:30:55.368
Don't say a word.

00:30:55.428 --> 00:30:57.119
Says the voice.

00:30:57.179 --> 00:30:59.370
It is a man's voice.

00:30:59.430 --> 00:31:01.501
You see this?

00:31:01.562 --> 00:31:03.972
He has a knife.

00:31:04.032 --> 00:31:07.474
He takes his hand away from my mouth.

00:31:07.534 --> 00:31:09.416
I see his face.

00:31:09.476 --> 00:31:12.461
It is the man in black.

00:31:12.521 --> 00:31:17.068
I come to Abu Simba and you are here too."

00:31:17.128 --> 00:31:18.520
He says.

00:31:18.580 --> 00:31:21.232
What are you doing here?

00:31:21.292 --> 00:31:25.506
I'm looking at the temple.

00:31:25.567 --> 00:31:27.728
Where's your friend?

00:31:27.788 --> 00:31:29.320
He asks.

00:31:29.380 --> 00:31:30.581
I don't know.

00:31:30.601 --> 00:31:32.162
I say.

00:31:32.222 --> 00:31:35.966
What are you doing here?

00:31:36.026 --> 00:31:38.385
Where's the statue?

00:31:38.445 --> 00:31:40.382
He smiles.

00:31:40.442 --> 00:31:42.914
It's in the bag.

00:31:42.974 --> 00:31:44.794
He says.

00:31:44.855 --> 00:31:47.986
What are you going to do with it?

00:31:48.047 --> 00:31:49.517
I ask.

00:31:49.577 --> 00:31:51.968
I'm going to sell it.

00:31:52.028 --> 00:31:53.649
He says.

00:31:53.709 --> 00:31:57.801
The man takes the statue out of the bag.

00:31:57.861 --> 00:32:00.442
He looks at it and laughs.

00:32:00.502 --> 00:32:06.266
Nefertari's temple is a good place to sell Nefertari's statue.

00:32:06.327 --> 00:32:09.258
It's a long way from Cairo.

00:32:09.318 --> 00:32:12.659
It's a long way for the police.

00:32:12.719 --> 00:32:16.740
He puts the statue in the back.

00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:20.761
A man is here to come here soon.

00:32:20.821 --> 00:32:23.711
He's going to give me a lot.

00:32:23.771 --> 00:32:27.742
I can a lot of things with that money.

00:32:27.802 --> 00:32:30.772
New clothes, fast cars.

00:32:30.832 --> 00:32:34.600
I like new clothes and fast cars.

00:32:34.660 --> 00:32:37.018
He laughs again.

00:32:37.078 --> 00:32:39.828
I see his yellow teeth.

00:32:39.888 --> 00:32:42.440
I don't like this man.

00:32:42.500 --> 00:32:44.550
His eyes are black.

00:32:44.610 --> 00:32:46.551
His hands are dirty.

00:32:46.611 --> 00:32:49.662
He is a bad man.

00:32:49.722 --> 00:32:55.104
But the question is, what do I do with you?

00:32:55.164 --> 00:32:57.055
He asks.

00:32:57.115 --> 00:32:59.376
I look at the ground.

00:32:59.436 --> 00:33:02.567
I look at the bag on the ground.

00:33:02.628 --> 00:33:05.074
He looks at me again.

00:33:05.134 --> 00:33:08.011
I'm going to tie you up."

00:33:08.072 --> 00:33:09.552
He says.

00:33:09.612 --> 00:33:14.786
I'm going to tie you up with this rope.

00:33:14.846 --> 00:33:18.237
He takes a rope from the bag.

00:33:18.297 --> 00:33:21.529
Then I am going to go to Spain.

00:33:21.549 --> 00:33:24.861
I like the food in Spain.

00:33:24.921 --> 00:33:27.212
Now, get over there.

00:33:27.232 --> 00:33:29.904
He pushes me.

00:33:29.964 --> 00:33:31.965
I fold the ground.

00:33:32.025 --> 00:33:34.417
My face is in the sand.

00:33:34.477 --> 00:33:37.539
I pick up sand in my hands.

00:33:37.600 --> 00:33:40.281
Get up, he says.

00:33:40.341 --> 00:33:42.602
Get up now.

00:33:42.663 --> 00:33:44.414
I stand up.

00:33:44.474 --> 00:33:46.275
He comes near me.

00:33:46.335 --> 00:33:49.386
I throw the sand at his face.

00:33:49.446 --> 00:33:52.458
I throw it into his eyes.

00:33:52.518 --> 00:33:56.381
The knife and the rope fall to the ground.

00:33:56.441 --> 00:33:59.272
He puts his hands to his eyes.

00:33:59.332 --> 00:34:02.423
He can't see.

00:34:02.483 --> 00:34:05.644
He shouts.

00:34:05.704 --> 00:34:07.966
I pick up the bag.

00:34:08.026 --> 00:34:10.947
I run to the front of the temple.

00:34:11.008 --> 00:34:12.888
Help!

00:34:12.948 --> 00:34:14.320
I shout.

00:34:14.380 --> 00:34:17.201
Help me!

00:34:17.261 --> 00:34:20.873
A man is standing in front of me.

00:34:20.934 --> 00:34:23.335
I can't see his face.

00:34:23.395 --> 00:34:26.516
Is it the bad man's friend?

00:34:26.577 --> 00:34:28.899
I run into the man.

00:34:28.959 --> 00:34:30.990
He falls to the ground.

00:34:31.050 --> 00:34:33.309
It's Mr. Johnson.

00:34:33.370 --> 00:34:35.859
And Kate is behind him.

00:34:35.919 --> 00:34:38.360
It's okay, Maddie.

00:34:38.420 --> 00:34:41.231
He says, it's okay.

00:34:41.291 --> 00:34:44.743
The police are here.

00:34:44.803 --> 00:34:49.715
Kate and I are in our English class.

00:34:49.775 --> 00:34:54.187
Mr. Johnson is reading our stories about Egypt.

00:34:54.247 --> 00:34:57.528
He stands up in front of the class.

00:34:57.588 --> 00:35:01.886
You are good writers, he says.

00:35:01.946 --> 00:35:08.578
I like your stories, but only one story can be the winner.

00:35:08.638 --> 00:35:11.060
He looks at us.

00:35:11.120 --> 00:35:13.932
And the winner is?

00:35:13.992 --> 00:35:16.813
He looks at us again.

00:35:16.874 --> 00:35:21.507
Land of Gold by Kate Wilkinson.

00:35:21.567 --> 00:35:25.840
It's a very good detective story, Kate.

00:35:25.900 --> 00:35:28.391
We smile at Kate.

00:35:28.452 --> 00:35:30.572
She smiles too.

00:35:30.632 --> 00:35:33.792
Thank you, she says.

00:35:33.852 --> 00:35:37.394
Where are we going to go next, Mr. Johnson?

00:35:37.454 --> 00:35:42.619
We're going to go to Russia next year, he says.

00:35:42.679 --> 00:35:45.542
Oh good, says Kate.

00:35:45.602 --> 00:35:47.863
I'm reading a book on Russia.

00:35:47.923 --> 00:35:52.146
The old buildings there have gold statues.

00:35:52.206 --> 00:35:55.069
Mr. Johnson smiles.

